    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d87">

                <pb facs="0189" n="79" xml:id="pg79"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">815.113/311: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Honduras</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Summerlin</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-07-12T17:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 12, 1928—5
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>62. Department’s telegram No. 52, June 20, 11 a.m., and your despatch No. 639,
                    June 21. What steps, if any, has the Government of Honduras taken to cooperate
                    in making effective in the future the embargo against contraband shipments to
                    Honduras?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
